  <Section width="narrow" id="who-qualifies">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who Qualifies for private health insurance?</h2>

        <p>The main eligibility criterion for employees is the <strong>Jahresarbeitsentgeltgrenze (JAEG)</strong>, commonly called the Versicherungspflichtgrenze. For 2026, this threshold is <strong>€77,400 gross annual income</strong>.</p>

        <p>Employees who earn above this threshold for the current calendar year can opt out of public health insurance and choose private health insurance. There is an additional rule: you must have exceeded the threshold for the previous year as well (or be starting a new job above the threshold). This prevents people from briefly spiking their income to switch.</p>

        <p>Three groups can always choose private health insurance regardless of income:</p>

            </div>
    <div class="aud-grid">
      <AudienceCard title="Self-employed &amp; freelancers" text="Genuinely self-employed people can choose private cover from day one, at any income level." href="/guide/for-freelancers">
        <svg slot="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="7" width="18" height="13" rx="2" /><path d="M9 7V5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2v2M3 13h18" /></svg>
      </AudienceCard>
      <AudienceCard title="Civil servants" text="Beihilfe covers 50 to 80 percent of medical costs, so private cover only fills the remainder at a reduced premium." href="/guide/who-qualifies">
