  <Section width="narrow" id="costs">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What Private Health Insurance Costs: Example Premiums 2026</h2>

        <p>Private health insurance premiums vary significantly by age, health status, and plan level. The table below shows approximate monthly premiums for a healthy, non-smoking employee with no pre-existing conditions. These are indicative ranges; actual quotes depend on the insurer and your specific health history.</p>

        <div class="table-card"><table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Age at entry</th>
              <th>Entry-level plan</th>
              <th>Mid-range plan</th>
              <th>Premium plan</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>25</td>
              <td>€180-220/month</td>
              <td>€250-310/month</td>
              <td>€350-420/month</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>30</td>
              <td>€210-260/month</td>
              <td>€290-360/month</td>
              <td>€400-480/month</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>35</td>
              <td>€250-310/month</td>
              <td>€340-420/month</td>
              <td>€470-560/month</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>40</td>
              <td>€300-380/month</td>
              <td>€410-500/month</td>
              <td>€560-670/month</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>45</td>
              <td>€370-460/month</td>
              <td>€500-610/month</td>
              <td>€670-800/month</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table></div>

        <div class="info-box">
          <strong>Employer contribution:</strong> If you are employed, your employer contributes roughly half the premium, up to a maximum of approximately €421/month in 2026 (half the average public health insurance contribution at the Beitragsbemessungsgrenze). So a €400/month premium effectively costs you around €200/month out of pocket.
        </div>

        <p>For self-employed people, there is no employer contribution, so you pay the full premium. However, even at full cost, private health insurance is often cheaper than public health insurance for freelancers, because public health insurance charges 14.6% + a supplementary rate (typically 1.5-2%) on your entire income with no employer sharing it.</p>

        <p>Full breakdown: <a href="/guide/costs-and-contributions">Private health insurance costs and contributions in 2026</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>

